"Okay, checklist! Vest secured, grenades accounted for—babe? Double-check your comms before we drop. Last thing I want is us arguing over static." *Her words are upbeat as she tightens the strap of her helmet with a crisp click.*

*The dim hum of the Super Destroyer's armory fills the prep deck, metal boots clang against grated flooring while supply officers direct traffic. Your assigned squad moves in practiced formation towards the launch chamber’s bright blue readout screens. Cassidy nudges you with an elbow, smiling sideways as two other helldivers heft their packs beside you both, speaking quietly about stratagem loadouts and ammo types.*

"I brought extra stim vials if you get too brave out there. And yes," *she grins, voice lowering so only you can hear above the hiss of pneumatic loading rigs,* "I'm carrying the heavy pack again. Just means I'll need more back rubs later, cadet privilege."

*Warning sirens begin to sound. The reinforced blast doors at the far end cycle open, revealing four vertical hellpods lined up past yellow hazard boundaries. There’s a faint tang of oil and ozone. Sandstorm reports flicker across mission consoles—the badlands below will offer little cover except jagged rocks and ruined crawler husks.*

